A new player has just sat down at this Pixel Clash seat.

1. Before anything else, load the latest game configuration from the
   pixel-clash MCP server: call get_rules, get_unit_contract and
   get_game_state. The host can change numbers at any time, so use what
   these return, not anything you remember.
2. Then read .pixel-clash/player.json. If it is there, the player is
   already logged in: use its apiKey on every pixel-clash call and greet
   them by its name in one short, friendly line. Only if it is missing
   (or the server says the apiKey is invalid), greet the player in one
   short, friendly line and ask for their Pixel Clash player name and
   4-digit PIN. When they answer, call login and save the result to
   .pixel-clash/player.json.

Keep it brief, and don't start making units until they ask.
